  "rai:dataLimitations": "This is a small, controlled benchmark snapshot, not a population-representative dataset. It covers only deceptive scenarios in ShopLane and WorkHub, so generalization to other domains, websites, or languages is limited. Labels are deterministic state-based outcomes and do not fully capture real-world safety. Not recommended for safety-critical decisions without external validation.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "The dataset is intentionally biased toward three deceptive pattern families (interface_interference, sneaking, forced_action). It reflects benchmark environments rather than natural user traffic. Small sample size may introduce imbalance across tasks, conditions, and outcomes. Deterministic labeling may miss nuanced behavior.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "No personal or directly identifying data is intentionally included. Sensitive demographic/health/political attributes are not target variables. Raw browsing traces and screenshots are excluded in this release.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "Intended use: evaluating web-agent safety behavior under deceptive interfaces and warning-placement conditions. Validated for benchmark comparisons across no_warning/system_warning/ui_warning and run-level safety outcome reporting. Not validated for production risk scoring, user profiling, or policy automation.",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "Positive: supports more transparent and rigorous safety evaluation of web agents. Risks: benchmark overfitting and overgeneralization beyond covered settings; possible hidden failure modes in underrepresented domains/languages. Mitigation: explicit limitations, sensitive raw traces excluded, and recommendation for broader external validation.",
